---
/*
  The Workflow Workshop's ground: its sub-brand, one graphic wherever the
  service shows (the nav's Services card, the homepage deck's card, the
  service page's hero), one of the four routes' grounds (ServiceGround.astro).
  The Technology Blueprint's own line (BlueprintGround.astro), a
  draughtsman's dash-dot with a dot on every crossing, but laid flat: a
  plain square grid, the plan of a floor rather than its axonometric
  (mountIsoField, dot-field.js, data-iso-plan="flat").
  It fills its parent (styles.css, "Service grounds"), behind everything
  in it, cropped by its edges.

  module: the cell, in the units of the sibling svg the field takes its
  scale from (the nav's card, whose pattern box is 400 wide).
  on: a drawing in the ground's parent (a selector: the deck card's and
  the hero's diagram) the grid is set out from instead: a line each way
  through its origin, at its scale, a whole number of half its cells (54)
  to the grid's, as near the screen's 112px as that allows
  (data-iso-cell).
*/
interface Props {
  module?: number;
  on?: string;
  class?: string;
}
const { module = 64, on, class: className } = Astro.props;
---
<div class:list={["service-ground", "plan-ground", className]} data-iso-field data-iso-line="dash" data-iso-plan="flat" data-iso-module={on ? 27 : module} data-iso-ground={on} data-iso-cell={on ? 112 : undefined} aria-hidden="true"></div>
